- The Labour Advisory Council is established by Ministerial Decree of 26 May 2021; 
- Regulation for the Establishment, Organization and Rules of Functioning of the Labour Advisory Council of the Republic of South Sudan adopted on 5 July 2021;
- LAC members appointed by Ministerial Decree of 26 May 2021;
- LAC established as mandated by Article 20 of the Labour Act, making explicit reference to "Advise the Office of the Labour Commissioner on issues arising from the activities of 
the International Labour Organization"


 - ILO developed TOR for international consultant;
- Consultant drafted Regulations and Rules with technical assistance of ILO NPC South Sudan, CO Addis Ababa, DWT for North Africa and headquarters;
- ILO organized and technically facilitated tripartite workshop discussing and approving draft regulation on 31 May and 1 June 2021
